Z||000006||DJRice||02-26-2001||08:20 PM||||If you really want to do this the easy way would be to:<P>1) Find one of the Fastback hotwheels cars which was called Ammo, because it was a 4x4 Fiero with missles and guns.  <P>2) Find a regular notchback Fiero hotwheels car<P>3) Drill out the rivits on both of them.  <P>4) Pull out the plastic shell that is the missles, guns, etc on the big fiero.  <P>5) Trim the plastic seat assy from the notchback fiero to fit the 4x4 body<P>6) Put the notchback base (chassis and wheels) on the fastback body.  <P>7) Find a way to hold it together (probably put a screw in where the rivit was)<P>8) Somewhere in there you should paint the fastback body to look like what you want it to.  Preferably before you put the thing together.  <P>The "Ammo" hot wheels typically sells for $10 if you can find one in the package.  It went by another name as well but I dont remember what it was.<P>Hope this gets you started<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000007||qwikgta||02-28-2001||11:58 PM||||I did a similar thing by drilling out the rivits and changing wheels on one of my Hotwheels Fieros.  Good luck<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||10
